{
 "about": "The handle sheet (ED1, editing design sections 2, 3 and 3B): the few true inputs of a world, a star and a system, each a handle with the part its strip opens on. Fields are kernel fields; values are SI except where `per` names the sheet constant a field is held in multiples of (surface water in Earth oceans). Figures are said by the units engine (figures.ts) with `kind` and `about`. `scale` is how the strip lays the value out. `refs` are the catalogued Solar System bodies (packs/base-sol ids) drawn as reference dots at Curious depth; this system's other worlds are drawn at every depth. `desks` are where the handle may be moved; Explore shows it read-only. This sheet moves into the base pack beside the units scheme (MP15) so a pack can add a handle for a field of its own. `results` are the kernel's results for a world (resolved_system's surface entry, flattened) that 'what followed' lists when they move. `box` is what a handle opens (design section 11F): the handle's own strip first, then `parts` (each a strip or a ring on a kernel field, shown from its `depth` up; `range` fixes a strip's ends in SI; `as` names how a ring reads its field, `true_anomaly_now` being the place round the orbit at the campaign's now), `chips` (one press, one set_value: `mirror` turns an angle to its mirror past 90 degrees, `flip` the sign, `lock` the day to the year, `resonance` the size to a period in step with a neighbour) and `results` (said under the box).",
